Description: Build the same container trees as i3 on move and swap
 Regolith binds the same keys to move left|down|up|right in both
 sessions, and window-management scripts use swap container with
 con_id. With the same keys and commands, sway built different layouts
 than i3, and the focus order in get_tree no longer led to the focused
 window after a move or a swap.
 .
 Moving into a neighbouring container now descends into it as i3 does:
 in a container split along the movement it takes the child nearest to
 where the container comes from, in any other container the most
 recently focused child, and stops at the first window. The container
 goes next to that window: before it when its parent is split along the
 movement and the move is right or down, after it otherwise. The focus
 order is updated as i3 does, and the focus path then leads to the
 focused window again.
 .
 Moving onto the adjacent output makes the container the first (right,
 down) or last (left, up) child of that output's visible workspace,
 whatever its layout.
 .
 Removing a redundant pair of nested split containers keeps the order of
 their children (it used to reverse it), with i3's focus order.
 .
 swap exchanges the two containers' places in the focus order as well,
 on any workspace or output. If both are on the focused workspace the
 focused window keeps the focus; otherwise, if the focus was in one of
 them, it moves to the container that took its place, keyboard included.
 This also fixes https://github.com/swaywm/sway/issues/9259.
 .
 Moving a lone window up or down on its workspace still changes the
 workspace orientation as before (i3 keeps it).
